      "comparison": "Both companies frame their business identity around technological leadership and innovation in high-performance computing and AI. NVIDIA explicitly states it has invested over $45.3 billion in R&D since inception to drive innovation (nvda_2024_1_P006_S002), while AMD describes itself as a 'high performance and adaptive computing leader' that drives innovation through technology and software leadership (amd_2024_1_P004_S002, amd_2024_1_P004_S003). Both disclosures emphasize that their technology powers data centers and AI applications, though NVIDIA highlights specific historical invention milestones (GPU, CUDA) and AMD highlights its broad portfolio solutions.",
