      "peer_disclosure_id": "amd_2024_1_D068",
      "relationship": "related_topic",
      "comparison": "NVIDIA identifies software as a critical component of its innovation strategy, noting that more than half of its engineers work on software and that it has built full software stacks like CUDA and AI Enterprise (nvda_2024_1_P006_S008, nvda_2024_1_P006_S011). In contrast, AMD's disclosure regarding ASIC competition focuses on hardware market dynamics rather than its own software R&D depth, though it acknowledges competition from ASICs which are often custom software-hardware integrations. The similarity lies in the recognition of the competitive landscape shaped by computing evolution, but the topics diverge in focus: NVIDIA details internal software R&D capacity, while AMD details external competitive threats from custom silicon.",
